      "slice": "HoldTableForReservation",
      "description": "Polls AutoSeatingCandidates for rows with autoSeatingOutcome 'Pending' and issues HoldTableForReservation for each. The processor picks the table itself: it walks table numbers 1 to 20 in ascending order and issues the command for the first one it has not already tried for this reservation, stopping as soon as one is accepted. A rejection (table blocked, or already held for that window) is expected and not an error - the processor moves on to the next table number. If every table rejects, the row stays 'Pending' and the staff seat the party manually. There is no seat-capacity data in this system, so numberOfPeople is carried for the staff to see but does not constrain the pick.",
      "context": "INTERNAL",
      "elementContext": "INTERNAL",
      "listElement": false,
      "todoList": false,
      "createsAggregate": false,
      "elementCopy": false,
      "sketched": false,
      "comments": []
    }
  ],
